{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789820676,"nonce":"CAro5be0QkYsJAU662WKxmO2p+4=","title":"SSA: a merge of a defined value and an undefined path collapsed to the value","message":"`read_variable_recursive` judged a merge on its real incomings only: undefs\nwere filtered out before the uniqueness test, so a block whose predecessors\nsupplied one defined value and one undef resolved to the defined value with\nno phi. That value need not dominate the block. At a loop header whose\npreheader supplies undef (a variable first assigned inside the loop) the\nheader's definition became the latch's value, defined inside the loop;\nreads of it after the loop, and OSR frame stores at the header, used a\nvalue from a non-dominating block. Cranelift refused the function\n(\"uses value arg from non-dominating blockN\") and the module body of the\narray conformance case fell back to the interpreter, which cannot run the\ngenerator's union.\n\nReproducer: `crates/zyntax_python/conformance/modules/array_module.py` at\nits full length; sections run alone passed because the shape needs the\nmodule body's later loops to read the variable.\n\nFix: undefs count as incomings. Only a set of nothing but undefs collapses\n(to an undef); a defined value beside an undef keeps a real phi, whose\nundef incoming Cranelift materialises as a zero.","files":null}]}